---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Card from '../components/Card.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import SoftPhoto from '../components/SoftPhoto.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="An old faith, seen in new light — about Roseville New Church, a Swedenborgian community in Sydney."
  currentPath="/about"
>
  <main class="container-prose px-6 md:px-8 pt-10 md:pt-14 pb-4">
    <div
      class="font-display font-semibold text-eyebrow tracking-eyebrow uppercase text-accent-primary mb-2.5"
    >
      ✦ About us
    </div>

    <article class="prose-rnc">
      <h1>An old faith, seen in new light</h1>
      <p>
        The Roseville New Church is a place of worship for those seeking to
        understand the Bible and the nature of God through the theological
        writings of Emanuel Swedenborg. We are the Sydney Society of the New
        Church, trading as Roseville New Church.
      </p>
      <p>
        We worship the Lord Jesus Christ as the one true God, in heaven and on
        earth. Our aim is to deepen our understanding of His love and wisdom, to
        share the distinctive doctrines of the New Church, and to help one
        another lead joyful and useful lives — in the present and the hereafter.
      </p>

      <h2>Our values</h2>
      <p>
        There does not exist the person the Lord does not love. It is the
        continual effort of the Lord to draw all people towards Himself, that
        each of us may experience heavenly states in this life and to eternity.
        Though difficult to comprehend, it is this expression of love we desire
        to manifest in the world as a New Church community.
      </p>

      <blockquote>
        “All who live well, of whatever religion, have a place in heaven.”
      </blockquote>
      <p class="quote-attr">Divine Providence 330</p>

      <h2>Understanding the Bible</h2>
      <p>
        On its surface the Bible can present a confusing picture of God —
        especially when its words and stories are taken only literally. Jesus
        often criticised people for missing the spirit of the law while keeping
        its letter. We read the Word with the help of Swedenborg's teaching that
        Scripture has an inner, spiritual sense: true lessons spoken in parable,
        clothing a deeper meaning so that it may be received and not falsified.
      </p>
      <p>
        With that knowledge we seek a greater understanding of the true nature
        of God and our purpose in this world and the next. You don't need to
        know anything about Swedenborg to visit — come as you are, ask anything,
        and stay for morning tea.
      </p>

      <h2>What to expect</h2>
      <p>
        Walking into a new place can feel intimidating. We want you to know you
        are welcome here — a warm community where everyone is accepted and
        valued.
      </p>
      <p>
        When you arrive you will find quiet contemplation with pre-service
        music. The service begins with an opening hymn. We provide a pamphlet
        with the order of service and the hymns for the day, so you always know
        what comes next.
      </p>
      <p>
        Afterwards we invite you to stay for refreshments and conversation. A
        pouch at the back of the sanctuary is there for free-will offerings to
        support the church; we do not pass a collection during the service, so
        please enjoy your first visit without any obligation to give.
      </p>
    </article>

    <!-- Soft place photos — secondary to the copy -->
    <div
      class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-[1.2fr_0.8fr] gap-3 sm:gap-4"
    >
      <SoftPhoto
        src="/images/church/exterior.jpg"
        alt="The brick church exterior at 2B Shirley Road, Roseville"
        aspect="aspect-[4/3] sm:aspect-[5/4]"
      />
      <SoftPhoto
        src="/images/church/stained-glass.jpg"
        alt="Stained glass window inside Roseville New Church"
        aspect="aspect-[4/3] sm:aspect-[5/4]"
      />
    </div>

    <div id="visit" class="scroll-mt-24 mt-6">
      <Card variant="tint" title="Come and see us">
        <p class="m-0">
          Worship on the <strong>1st and 3rd Sundays</strong> of each month at
          <strong>10am</strong>.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 mb-0">
          2B Shirley Rd, Roseville NSW 2069 — two minutes' walk from Roseville
          station. The Swedenborg Centre is next door at 4 Shirley Rd.
        </p>
        <div slot="footer" class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <Button
            href="https://maps.google.com/?q=2B+Shirley+Rd,+Roseville+NSW+2069"
          >
            Get directions
          </Button>
          <Button variant="secondary" href="tel:+61294167026">
            Call the church office
          </Button>
        </div>
      </Card>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
